{
 "manufacturer": "Lovato Electric",
 "manufacturer_slug": "lovato-electric",
 "model": "ATL610 automatic transfer switch controller",
 "model_slug": "atl610",
 "short_model": "ATL610",
 "aliases": [
  "ATL610",
  "ATL 610",
  "EXP1012",
  "EXP1013"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Transfer switch",
 "applies_to": "ATL610 ATS controller via the optical port or an EXP1010/1011/1012/1013 communication module, per protocol document I428 GB I 09 22.",
 "summary": "The ATL610 is Lovato's two-line automatic transfer switch controller for mains/mains or mains/generator changeover. It speaks Modbus RTU, ASCII or TCP through its optical port or plug-in USB, RS-232, RS-485 and Ethernet modules. This map covers both lines' voltages and frequencies, battery voltage, run-time and operation counters, the 32-bit alarm word, line and breaker status words, controller status, and the mode, breaker, generator and reset commands.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU",
  "ASCII",
  "TCP"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baud": 9600,
  "parity": "None",
  "data_bits": 8,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": 1001
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "1-based",
  "note": "The tables print hex addresses one higher than the address in the request; the document says the query address must be decreased by one, its RTU example reads breaker 1 switching alarms (table 3Ah) by sending 00 39, and the event-log examples show 5030h - 1 = 502Fh. Addresses here are already reduced by one."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "ATL610 Automatic transfer switch controller - Communication protocol Modbus",
  "doc_number": "I428 GB I 09 22",
  "revision_date": "2022-09",
  "url": "https://datasheet.lovatoelectric.com/DOWNLOAD/Technical/TechInstructions/31.%20COMMUTATORI%20DI%20RETE%20AUTOMATICI/I428IGB09_22.pdf",
  "pages": "pp. 1-3 (settings, functions, examples), pp. 7-10 (Tables 2-4)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Measures and status words are read with function 03 or 04 (same data) and are listed as input registers. Commands are written with function 06; function 06 only works on addresses above 1000h.",
  "Word order: the RTU example returns 00 00 00 07 for 7 switching alarms, so the high word comes first (ABCD).",
  "Units as printed: voltages in whole volts, frequency Hz/10, battery VDC/10, times in seconds.",
  "The ASCII example in the document calls the register at 0Ch an 'L3 current', which does not match the ATL610 table (0Ch is LINE 1 L3-L1 voltage); the label looks copied from another product. Its frame (00 0B for 0Ch) still follows the minus-one rule.",
  "Left out: minimum/maximum battery voltage (printed in V while the live value is VDC/10), maintenance hours and operations-to-maintenance (unit 'nr' with no clear meaning), generic counters CNT1-4 and LIM bits (user-defined), the 2-word device global status at 2210h ('Unsigned integer' over 2 words), and the real-time clock registers.",
  "Left out because the document contradicts itself: digital outputs status (table says 2140h, bit legend says 2072h) and input functions status (table says 2078h with 2 words, legend says 2178h). The two 'Frontal LED status' words 207Eh/207Fh have no bit legend.",
  "Remote variables REM1-REM8 are at 4F00h-4F07h (only REM1 and REM2 listed): write AAh to set, BBh to clear."
 ],
